  Release packages include CEF and Chromium. They are downloaded at build time and are not stored in this repository.
  CEF is licensed under a BSD-style license. Chromium and its components carry their own licenses.
  See the credits file shipped inside each package.
  libcef contains FFmpeg and other code under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) version 2.1 or later. The
  LGPL 2.1 text is in FFmpeg's entry in that credits file. Release packages ship the CEF project's own build, unmodified,
  from https://cef-builds.spotifycdn.com, with its default settings, which leave the proprietary codecs (H.264, AAC)
  out. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt names the exact CEF and Chromium version.
  Written offer: for three years from the date you received a release package, Nexus Laboratories, Inc. will give
  anyone who asks a complete machine-readable copy of the corresponding source code of the CEF and Chromium version in
